1
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:04,760
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:07,100
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

3
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:13,540
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

4
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:29,540
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

5
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,880
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

6
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:42,800
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

7
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,420
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

8
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:49,580
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

9
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:53,040
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

10
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:56,420
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

11
00:00:56,420 --> 00:01:00,000
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,140
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

13
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:09,840
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

14
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:14,940
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

15
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:16,820
...kaeru basho mo nai no

16
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:20,120
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

17
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:23,600
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

18
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:27,260
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

19
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,800
In search of the dark secrets
of the Philosopher's Stone,

20
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,800
Ed and Al break into the
supposedly deserted Fifth Laboratory.

21
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,760
There they encounter
two guards who, like Al,

22
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:46,400
have had their souls
bonded to suits of armor.

23
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:51,960
In the course of their fight, Al's
opponent, 66, plants suspicions in his mind.

24
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:55,800
Al begins to wonder if he is a
counterfeit soul created by Ed,

25
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,800
and bonded to a suit of armor to
become the older boy's biddable puppet.

26
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:07,200
ROSS: Looks like you can sit up now, huh?

27
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:09,520
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

28
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:11,480
What happened with the Fifth Laboratory?

29
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,800
Well, it, um...

30
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:16,340
Somebody blew up the building and
there's nothing left of it now but rubble.

31
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:18,840
Damn it!
You mean they wiped out everything?

32
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,800
That didn't feel good.

33
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,800
This isn't fair...

34
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,800
Do you know how close I
was to finding out the truth?

35
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:31,100
This is no time for me to
be lying around in a hospital.

36
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:32,420
BOTH: Hm.

37
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,400
BOTH: Fullmetal Alchemist, sir!

38
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:36,060
Hm?

39
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,480
We do apologize in advance for this!

40
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:39,380
Huh?

41
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:41,800
[SMACK]

42
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:48,800
You acted like a selfish child.

43
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:51,800
You only escaped with your
life because you were lucky.

44
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:55,800
You don't have to do everything
all on your own, you know.

45
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,800
You can lean on other people.

46
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:01,800
Like us.

47
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:04,800
Not all adults are the enemy.
You can trust us.

48
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:10,700
BOTH: That's all!

49
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:13,540
Please forgive our abusive
words and conduct, sir!

50
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:15,240
It will not happen again!

51
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:15,860
Uh...

52
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,800
No, you're right.

53
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,080
I should be apologizing.

54
00:03:22,050 --> 00:03:24,800
My punishment...
for slapping you.

55
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:25,800
Huh?

56
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,240
Nothing, I had it coming.

57
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,780
[RELIEVED SOUNDS]

58
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,800
What's got you two so scared of me?

59
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:35,000
- State-certified alchemists carry a military rank equivalent to that of a Major.
- Mm-hmm.

60
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,380
Don't worry about it.

61
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:39,360
I didn't get my certification
so people would kiss up to me.

62
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:42,440
You don't have to talk to me
like I'm a high-ranking officer.

63
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:43,800
Really? Oh!

64
00:03:43,830 --> 00:03:46,220
Ah, I guess we were
scared of the brat for nothing.

65
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,100
They adjust quickly...

66
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:51,300
Um, where's Al? I haven't seen him.

67
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:53,480
Alphonse got his own lecture earlier.

68
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:56,100
But I was the one who did the slapping.

69
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,720
[PAINED LAUGHTER]

70
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:00,640
I almost forgot.

71
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:03,840
I have an even less pleasant
lecture in store for me today.

72
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:08,960
[PHONE RINGING]

73
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:11,680
Hello? Rockbell Prosthetic Glam Outfitters.

74
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:14,380
Oh, Ed.

75
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:17,340
Since when do you ever bother to call us, is something wrong?

76
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:18,200
Yeah...

77
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:19,800
Here's the deal.

78
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:24,640
I hate to ask you, but...do you think you
could make a service call out to Central for me?

79
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:25,800
A service call?

80
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:26,600
Yeah.

81
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:28,520
My right arm's messed up again.

82
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,860
I can move the fingers,
but that's about it.

83
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:32,120
I can't lift the arm at all.

84
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:32,800
[GASPS]

85
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,880
[NERVOUS LAUGH]

86
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:40,180
- Yeah, that sounds about right.
- Huh?

87
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:41,800
Nothing! Just talking to myself.

88
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:44,380
So, what were you doing
when the arm stopped working?

89
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,800
Uh... [GULPS]

90
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,700
I was in a really rough fight.

91
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:51,500
You did it again, moron!

92
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:55,880
How could you treat my precious automail like that, Alchemy Freak?!

93
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,300
Uh, are you there?

94
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:03,640
Hello, Winry.

95
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,420
Guess I've got no choice.

96
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:06,600
Tell me how to get there.

97
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,420
ED: You're sure in a good mood today.

98
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:13,800
I thought you were going to—you know what? Never mind. Forget it.

99
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,800
Yeah.

100
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:15,800
Yep.

101
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,700
Sorry again, and thanks.

102
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:18,500
Right.

103
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,820
Goodbye.

104
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:21,840
[EXHALES]

105
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:23,120
Aw, was that your girlfriend?

106
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:25,680
My girlfriend?! No way!

107
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,560
It's nothing to be embarrassed about.

108
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:31,000
When I was your age, I had a
different girlfriend every week.

109
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:31,720
Hmm?

110
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,400
What are you doing sitting
there in the dark by yourself?

111
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:35,860
Hey.

112
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:37,020
Hey,  Al.

113
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:38,540
Brother.

114
00:05:38,650 --> 00:05:40,820
You know you can come to the room, right?

115
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,760
I'll be there in a little while.

116
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,800
You go on ahead.

117
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:51,800
Okay.

118
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:02,960
[SOFT, MECHANICAL FOOTSTEPS]

119
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:12,460
[GIGGLE]

120
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:13,560
Bye!

121
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:23,580
Are you sure you're not a puppet
created by your so-called brother?

122
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:31,800
[BELLS RINGING]

123
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,400
Ugh, that left me really sore.

124
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:37,320
I don't understand how Ed
and Al can ride on these things.

125
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:42,040
Ed said to look near the west exit.

126
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:45,560
There'd be someone familiar there
who I'd recognize right away.

127
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:49,160
Hello, Major Armstrong, it's Winry!

128
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:53,600
Hello, Miss Winry. Did you have a pleasant trip?

129
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:57,320
Where are those stupid Elric brothers?

130
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,200
[GULPS]

131
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:00,680
Well, you see...

132
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:01,800
Hmm?

133
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:05,760
[INDISCERNIBLE]

134
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,800
The hospital? What happened?!

135
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:13,560
ED: Well, that didn't take long.

136
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:17,300
You're gonna charge me an
express service fee now, aren't you?

137
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:21,100
No, I... I won't
charge you for this.

138
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:23,560
I didn't do a good enough job on your automail last time.

139
00:07:25,150 --> 00:07:26,800
And now you're badly injured.

140
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:33,520
It's not your fault! You can't blame yourself for this!

141
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:35,960
I broke it because I was being reckless!

142
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:39,720
Your repairs were flawless as ever! This was all my fault!

143
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,620
WINRY: He has no idea...

144
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:44,160
He never noticed that I
forgot to put in that screw.

145
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:46,640
Besides, if my arm hadn't
broken when it did, I would have

146
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:49,100
kept fighting and then I would
have been hurt even worse!

147
00:07:49,250 --> 00:07:50,800
So don't worry about it, okay?

148
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,800
Okay?

149
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,800
WINRY: So it turned out all right?

150
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:55,540
[LAUGHS]

151
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:58,380
Well, then, let's go ahead and get right down to business, shall we?

152
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:01,060
I'll have to charge you the
usual rush order fee, of course.

153
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:01,800
Huh?

154
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:02,800
Hmm?

155
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:06,540
You didn't drink your milk.

156
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:09,500
Why should I?

157
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:10,560
I hate it.

158
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:14,760
You're going to be small and stunted
forever if you keep using that stupid excuse!

159
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,740
Shut up!

160
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,980
I don't have to drink it if I don't wanna!

161
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:20,840
You sound like a spoiled little brat, Edward Elric!

162
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:23,980
ROSS: Every growing boy needs his milk.

163
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,040
BROSH: Yeah, you want the girls to like ya, don't you?

164
00:08:27,850 --> 00:08:30,800
- Was that Al?
- Hmm?

165
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:37,840
ED: I don't get it.

166
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:39,520
Al's been acting really weird lately.

167
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:42,040
WINRY: Weird how?

168
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:47,240
Just seems like something's
been bothering him.

169
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:05,300
Are you sure you're not a puppet
created by your so-called brother?

170
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:06,800
Just accept it.

171
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:08,060
You'll feel better.

172
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:09,220
[MIRROR CRACKS]

173
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:18,020
WINRY: Okay! You're all set.

174
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:20,380
[GROANS] Well done!

175
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,760
Ah, it feels good to have it back.

176
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,620
Wow, thanks a lot.

177
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:26,460
Sure, no problem.

178
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:27,260
[DOOR OPENS]
Hm?

179
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:28,900
Yo, Ed, my boy!

180
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Is it true you brought a pretty blonde
girl into your room to service you?

181
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:36,940
She's my automail mechanic, that's all! Nothing more!

182
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:38,220
Oh, I see.

183
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,540
You've seduced your mechanic, have you?

184
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:40,760
[SCREAMS]

185
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:44,000
That isn't what I said at all! Were you even listening to me?!

186
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:47,120
Maes Hughes, I'm pleased
to meet you, young lady.

187
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,020
You too, I'm Winry Rockbell.

188
00:09:49,220 --> 00:09:50,460
Nice to see you, Hughes.

189
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:52,460
But don't you have work to do?

190
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,960
Nope, it's all under control.

191
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:56,060
I gave Sheska some overtime.

192
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:58,160
ED: You're a real jerk, aren't you?

193
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,160
Oh, yeah, and I think you'll be happy to know...

194
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:03,840
I just found out you and Al shouldn't need to be kept
under guard for too much longer.

195
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,800
ED: Great!
WINRY: What'd you say?

196
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:07,500
Hold on just a second!

197
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:10,400
How much trouble have you
gotten yourself into this time?

198
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:13,800
Uh, well, you see, it's...

199
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:18,420
Well, it's nothing that concerns you.

200
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:27,140
Of course not.

201
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:28,900
I don't know why I bother to try.

202
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,560
It's not like you'll talk to me anyway.

203
00:10:32,780 --> 00:10:34,220
Fine, I'll see you tomorrow.

204
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,340
I have to go and see if I
can find some place to stay tonight.

205
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:41,580
Come on, no need for that. Why don't you spend the night at my place?

206
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:42,880
Really?

207
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:43,720
Yes, of course.

208
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:46,200
My wife and daughter will
be delighted to have you.

209
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:48,540
- Oh no, I—
- It's settled. Come on, come on.

210
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:50,320
Here, let me take that.

211
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,200
Oh, I've got it! Let's go!

212
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:54,560
- Do you really have to drag me?
- [LAUGHING]

213
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:01,660
[POPPING]
[LAUGHTER]

214
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:03,960
Happy birthday, Elicia!

215
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:07,480
[CHEERING]

216
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:11,600
Um, you don't mind me asking, Mr. Hughes, what is this all about?

217
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,800
I'm so glad you asked that, Miss Winry.

218
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:17,120
Today happens to be my
darling little Elicia's birthday!

219
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:18,580
Yeah, my birthday!

220
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:20,800
[LAUGHING]

221
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:23,560
That's exciting.
How old are you now, Elicia?

222
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:24,700
I'm two!

223
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:28,480
No, I'm three!

224
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:32,040
Oh how adorable!

225
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,180
Fullmetal Alchemist.

226
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:37,260
Fullmetal Alchemist

227
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:43,760
I've known the Elrics for about
as long as I can remember.

228
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:46,280
We grew up together.
They're like my brothers.

229
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:49,700
And I'm sure knowing those two,
they must give you plenty to worry about.

230
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:51,480
That's an understatement.

231
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:56,260
When they finally came back for a visit, it
was because Ed's arm was all busted up.

232
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:02,800
And now he calls me out here because
he's been seriously injured again.

233
00:12:03,740 --> 00:12:05,800
Something's bothering Al, too.

234
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:09,170
They keep their mouths shut, though.

235
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:11,460
They don't ever tell me what's going on.

236
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:14,800
It's just like when they left
Resembool for the first time.

237
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,930
HUGHES: Maybe nothing needed to be said.

238
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:21,800
You know these boys, Winry.

239
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:25,040
It's possible they thought you'd
understand without them saying anything.

240
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,500
Maybe.

241
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:32,980
But there are some things
that I actually need to be told.

242
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:36,440
Just what am I going to do with you?

243
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:41,800
In general, men prefer to let their
actions speak instead of words.

244
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:44,800
When they're in pain, they don't
want to burden anyone with it.

245
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,320
Not if they can help it.

246
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:49,080
They don't want anyone to worry about them.

247
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:50,800
That's how they are.

248
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:56,980
Even so, there may come a
time when they'll ask for your help.

249
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:01,380
And when they do, I know
that you'll be there for them.

250
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:03,800
Isn't that enough?

251
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:09,260
Elicia, we wanna play! Let's go!

252
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,940
Will you put me down now?

253
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:12,800
WINRY: Okay, down you go.

254
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:14,940
Hey, you get away from her!

255
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:16,800
Elicia wants to play with me, not you!

256
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:20,440
She's quite the heartbreaker
already, isn't she?

257
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:22,440
[GUN COCKING]

258
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,640
Listen up, boys.

259
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:27,800
You try anything with my
daughter, and you will answer to me.

260
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,800
Your actions speak too loudly!

261
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:36,800
GRACIA: Are you sure you have to go?

262
00:13:36,850 --> 00:13:39,800
You're more than welcome to stay
with us for as long as you're in town.

263
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:42,680
I don't want to put you out
more than I have already.

264
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:47,520
Elicia's gotten very attached to you.

265
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:48,940
[LAUGHS]

266
00:13:48,940 --> 00:13:51,800
Well, would you look at that!
The two of you could be sisters.

267
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:56,800
Sissy! Be safe, okay?
And come back and visit me real soon!

268
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:59,800
It's settled.
You're staying with us again tonight.

269
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:03,660
[BOTH GIGGLING]

270
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:06,480
It looks like I found
myself a little sister.

271
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:16,800
So we meet again, you little bastard.
I'm not gonna drink you.

272
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:21,800
Brother, you have a living
body that needs nourishment.

273
00:14:22,530 --> 00:14:23,800
You have to drink it.

274
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,800
I don't have to if I don't want to.

275
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:30,800
It may not look like it, but I have grown some.

276
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:33,240
But everyone still calls me a pipsqueak.

277
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,380
I wish I was like you, Al.

278
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,800
You've got such a big body now.

279
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:46,480
It's not like I asked
for this body, brother!

280
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:52,340
Sorry. You're right.
It's my fault that it happened.

281
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:57,300
But I'll make it right. I'll get you
back into your real body. You'll see, Al.

282
00:14:57,300 --> 00:15:00,020
AL: That's what you always say,
but you don't know that for sure!

283
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:03,800
L-look, I promise I'm gonna get you back.
Believe me, Al. I'll do it.

284
00:15:03,850 --> 00:15:04,900
Believe you?

285
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:08,800
How am I supposed to believe
anything when I'm stuck in this body?

286
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:11,240
What should I believe in? My memories?

287
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:15,800
Memories are just scraps of information that
can be made up as easily as anything else.

288
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:18,260
Al, what are you talking about?

289
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:21,800
Do you remember when you said there
was something you were afraid to tell me?

290
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:25,500
I think...
I think I might know what it was.

291
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:31,800
Maybe you wanted to say that my soul and my memories
are really artificial constructions you created!

292
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:40,800
You... Winry and Granny... You've
been lying to me all along, haven't you?

293
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:43,220
What do you have to
say for yourself, brother?

294
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:50,260
ED: Is that what you really think?
Have you believed that all this time?

295
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:51,160
[GASP]

296
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:57,180
So, are you finished?
Or is there more you wanted to say?

297
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:03,800
Okay.

298
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,500
Don't go.

299
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:17,380
Ed!

300
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:21,580
WINRY: Al, you...

301
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:24,240
...Moron!

302
00:16:24,260 --> 00:16:25,280
[CLANG]

303
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,780
ALL: Ah!

304
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:29,320
Where did that come from?!

305
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,800
[PANTING]

306
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,420
[GASPS] Winry?!

307
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:37,440
You idiot!

308
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:38,520
[CLANG]

309
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:40,580
You have no idea how Ed feels!

310
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:44,600
Do you know what he was
so afraid to talk to you about?

311
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:49,760
He wants to know if you blame him
for what happened to your body, Al!

312
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:55,020
It's all my fault.
Al lost his body and it's all my fault.

313
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:58,480
He can't eat anymore, he can't
sleep, he can't feel cold or warm.

314
00:16:58,540 --> 00:17:02,800
He's my little brother and I'm supposed to protect him
and I did this and—[SOBBING]

315
00:17:02,950 --> 00:17:04,800
How could he ever forgive me?

316
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:07,700
Al isn't the type of boy who would resent you for this.

317
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:09,740
Just ask him and I'm sure you'll see.

318
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:12,480
No. I'm... I'm too afraid.

319
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:15,180
I'm too scared of what he'll say.

320
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:17,540
[CLANGING]

321
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:23,460
And then... you idiot! You said that!

322
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:27,140
Whoever'd do something like that?

323
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:32,120
Who would be prepared to risk his own
life to create a fake brother?

324
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:35,640
Don't you get it? [SNIFFLES]

325
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:39,800
All the two of you have left... is each other.

326
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,800
Now! Go get your brother!

327
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,960
- Start running!
- Right!

328
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:06,340
- Bro—
- You know something, Al?

329
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:09,800
We haven't had a good fight in a while.
I'm starting to get flabby.

330
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:10,800
Huh?

331
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,800
Huh? Hey!

332
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,800
Hold on, brother!

333
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:27,100
Stop!

334
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:31,800
Your wounds haven't healed enough for this!

335
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:42,500
I beat you! The first time I ever won!

336
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:47,140
It wasn't a fair fight, brother.

337
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:50,240
Don't give me that.
A win is a win and you know it, Al.

338
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:55,140
We've always fought like this.
Ever since we were really little.

339
00:18:56,350 --> 00:19:00,180
Now that I think about it, we've fought
over some really stupid things, haven't we?

340
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:03,740
Definitely. Like who would
get the top and bottom bunks.

341
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:04,800
Yeah.

342
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:07,000
AL: We fought over candy a lot too, huh?

343
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,720
ED: And that toy, you remember?

344
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:12,080
AL: I won that one.
And when we played in the rain river too.

345
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:14,800
ED: Oh yeah. You shoved me into the water.

346
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:16,800
AL: And that fight we had during our training?

347
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:19,310
ED: Teacher said we were
being too loud, then she beat

348
00:19:19,330 --> 00:19:21,800
us up herself. Why don't
we call that one a draw?

349
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:25,120
AL: We even fought over which one
of us would marry Winry someday.

350
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:27,040
ED: What?! I don't remember that one.

351
00:19:27,060 --> 00:19:29,820
AL: I won the fight, but she shot me down.

352
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,600
ED: Oh...did she?

353
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,640
You're telling me that all
those memories are lies?

354
00:19:42,980 --> 00:19:43,900
AL: Sorry.

355
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:47,980
ED: And your determination to be whole again
to get your body back no matter what...

356
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:49,600
That's a lie too?

357
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:52,800
AL: No, it's not a lie.
ED: That's Right

358
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:55,360
We're in this together, all the way.

359
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:58,120
And forget that, we're
gonna keep pushing forward.

360
00:19:58,620 --> 00:20:03,060
We'll make ourselves stronger, faster,
and better until we get our bodies back.

361
00:20:03,380 --> 00:20:05,100
[AL CHUCKLES] And the milk?

362
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:08,800
ED: Milk?! Fine. I'll drink...a little.

363
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:10,940
[BOTH LAUGHING]

364
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:12,800
ED: Whatever it takes, brother.
AL: Mm!

365
00:20:14,740 --> 00:20:16,040
Mr. Hughes?

366
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:20,800
Maybe you don't have to hear something out loud,
but it sure is helpful sometimes.

367
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,740
I guess it is.

368
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:42,800
My brother...

369
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:44,960
Master...

370
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:47,080
They're gone. All gone.

371
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,680
Hey!

372
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:52,080
You don't look like an Ishvalan.
Who are you?

373
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:56,160
KIMBLEE: Oh my, where are my manners?
I should have introduced myself.

374
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:59,220
I'm a State Alchemist
sent here by the military.

375
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:02,380
I've been sent to
exterminate this sector.

376
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:11,780
Hey, you're awake!

377
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:13,680
Where am I?

378
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:17,480
In a slum outside of East City.
You're among friends now.

379
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:21,080
Who are you? You, old man.

380
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:24,760
Me? Why, I'm a man of
Ishvala, just as you are, son.

381
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:29,080
There's nothing to worry about here.
I won't sell out one of my own.

382
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:33,060
Are we the only ones here?
Are there other Ishvalan survivors?

383
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:35,220
Yes, indeed there are.

384
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:39,620
A run-down slum such as this may
bear no resemblance to our ancestral home,

385
00:21:39,780 --> 00:21:42,880
But you know what they
say, the world is God's bosom.

386
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:46,800
Our great, loving God Ishvala. Am I right? [CHUCKLES]

387
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:49,540
Yes, you certainly are.

388
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:52,080
You can't, you're not ready!

389
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:55,400
We found you
floating in the sewers. You were hurt bad.

390
00:22:03,840 --> 00:22:07,560
Boy, my right arm.
Did I lose it or is it still with me?

391
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:10,040
Yeah, it's still there, mister.
It should be fine.

392
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:15,920
Your tattoo...it's really amazing.

393
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:24,800
Yes, it's important to me.
A precious gift from my family.

394
00:22:28,380 --> 00:22:34,200
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

395
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:39,500
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

396
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:45,260
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

397
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:50,400
futari yorisotta

398
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:58,660
Muri na egao no ura

399
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:04,040
nobita kage o kakumau

400
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:13,420
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

401
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:22,640
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

402
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:31,480
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

403
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:35,780
zenbu wakatte'tan da

404
00:23:35,860 --> 00:23:41,340
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

405
00:23:41,340 --> 00:23:46,540
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

406
00:23:46,540 --> 00:23:51,980
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

407
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:57,040
futari arukidasu

408
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:02,420
A good friend became
a comrade-in-arms,

409
00:24:02,600 --> 00:24:05,460
and over time, his presence was taken for granted.

410
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:10,920
Although the future they once dreamed of
became bleaker than they had ever imagined,

411
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:15,120
this good friend was always there
by his side, where he belonged.

412
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:18,980
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

413
00:24:19,820 --> 00:24:22,980
Episode 10: Separate Destinations.

414
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:28,380
A friend whose presence comes as naturally
as breathing can never be replaced.
